# Slice Execution Packet Template

## Purpose

Turn one approved Slice into a bounded packet a receiving agent can execute without reconstructing the Campaign from chat history.

## Write Here When

Use for an explicit agent/session/machine transfer or cold executor. It may accompany an Exchange or generic handoff but replaces neither contract.

## Do Not Use For

Do not create a second live checklist, expand authority, summarize unverified claims as fact, or combine independent Slices. Stop after the named Slice(s) and gates.

## Format And Profile Selection

- `compact`: target 350–700 tokens when the Slice is narrow, capsule/index is current, and context is constrained or familiarity is high.
- `expanded`: target 700–1,200 tokens excluding linked sources for a cold receiver, shared-file hotspots, high risk, platform boundaries, or previous regressions.
- `auto`: receiver selects, records the choice and one-sentence reason, and loads expanded fields or stops if compact leaves ambiguity.

Both profiles carry identical behavior, authority, checks, deliverables, and stop conditions. Expanded adds section-level reading reasons, prerequisite evidence, shared consumers, and conditional failure routes.

Compact normally names at most five inspect-first sources and expanded at most ten; conditional sources load only on their trigger. Narrow the Slice or explain a mandatory larger set.

